			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Introduce stub health probe commands for backend services\n\nAdd a new suite of Tauri commands under `Source/Binary/IPC/HealthCommand` to expose readiness states for internal and sidecar services to the Wind frontend. This includes `cocoon_debug_service_health`, `cocoon_extension_host_health`, and `cocoon_search_service_health` for the extension host subsystem, alongside a generic `shared_process_service_health` dispatcher.\n\nThe implementation follows the project's PascalCase naming conventions for command registration while intentionally retaining snake_case function names to align with the `SharedProcessProxy` invoker in the Wind service layer. `cocoon_search_service_health` and `shared_process_service_health` currently return `true` to signal filesystem readiness or known service availability, whereas DAP and extension host probes return `false` as stubs pending the actual gRPC wire-up with Cocoon.\n\nThis establishes the initial IPC interface for service liveness monitoring, allowing the frontend to conditionally enable features based on backend component status without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "ba9d963cc9fe42079f53c1ca6177d9ad57ae0ca8"
		},
