				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1164,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement cross-platform process introspection commands\n\nAdd a suite of new Tauri commands within `Binary/IPC/ProcessCommand` to expose essential runtime environment data to the Wind frontend. These commands include `ProcessGetArch`, `ProcessGetPlatform`, `ProcessGetPid`, `ProcessGetExecPath`, `ProcessGetShellEnv`, and `ProcessGetMemoryInfo`.\n\nThe implementation bridges the gap between Rust's native system calls and VS Code's Node-style expectations. `ProcessGetPlatform` normalizes OS names (e.g., mapping `macos` to `darwin`), while `ProcessGetMemoryInfo` executes platform-specific probes (`ps` on macOS, `tasklist` on Windows, `/proc/self/statm` on Linux) to calculate private, shared, and resident set memory in bytes. All commands return results as `Result` types with graceful fallbacks (zeroed values or empty maps) if underlying system queries fail, ensuring the renderer remains stable even during environment anomalies.\n\nThis establishes the foundational IPC layer for the `ProcessPolyfill` service, allowing the editor to correctly identify the host architecture, platform, and resource constraints without relying on external Node.js shims.",
			"SHA": "e1803d15dcd25dea32c474b7aa749ec60a9954da"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:05:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1157,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Introduce modular PostHog telemetry plugin\n\nAtomize the PostHog telemetry integration into a dedicated plugin structure within `Binary/Build/PostHogPlugin`. This introduces a strict separation of concerns: `CaptureAllowed` acts as a compile-time and env-var gate to disable telemetry in non-debug builds; `Initialize` bootstraps the singleton `Client` instance and emits the session start event; `CaptureEvent` handles the core logic of stamping standard metadata (`$app`, `$component`) before dispatching; and specific wrappers (`CaptureError`, `CaptureIPC`) provide typed instrumentation for error logging and gRPC method tracing.\n\nThe implementation adheres to project naming conventions with dedicated `Fn::Fn` modules and uses `env!` macros to bake credentials (`Authorize`, `Beam`, `Report`) from `.env.Land.PostHog` at compile time, ensuring a clean checkout builds without runtime dependency on external secrets. This lays the foundation for observability within the Mountain backend without blocking the primary IPC or UI loops.",
			"SHA": "20a80336a80f6ead98f874736b87a6cc20ecfdf6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:05:39Z",
